From: fxtec-pro1x-guix
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: nxp-nci: the board's clocks; sm6115-pro1x: the NFC clock

The Pro1X's NXP PN557 answers on I2C but finds no tag: its RF never
starts.  The stock vendor partition's libnfc-nxp.conf says it runs on
an external 19.2 MHz clock (NXP_SYS_CLK_SRC_SEL=0x01, PLL;
NXP_SYS_CLK_FREQ_SEL=0x02), which it asks for on its clock request line,
GPIO 86.  The vendor tree pulls that line up; it was pulled down here.

nxp-nci gets and enables the clocks a board names, if any (none before:
no change for other boards).  The Pro1X names both pin-controlled RF
clocks of the RPM, which one feeds the controller is not known, and
pulls GPIO 86 up.

Ours (fxtec-pro1x-guix, 2026-11-23).  Untested: for the CI build.

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
index ba5e228..93fd141 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm6115-fxtec-pro1x.dts
@@ -359,6 +359,15 @@
 		interrupts = <70 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
 		enable-gpios = <&tlmm 69 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
 		firmware-gpios = <&tlmm 31 GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH>;
+		/*
+		 * The controller runs on a 19.2 MHz clock from the PMIC, asked
+		 * for on its clock request line (the vendor HAL's
+		 * NXP_SYS_CLK_SRC_SEL: PLL).  Both pin-controlled RF clocks
+		 * are kept voted, as it is not known which one feeds it.
+		 */
+		clocks = <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_RF_CLK1_PIN>, <&rpmcc RPM_SMD_RF_CLK2_PIN>;
+		pinctrl-0 = <&nfc_clk_req>;
+		pinctrl-names = "default";
 	};
 
 	haptics: haptics@58 {
@@ -1742,4 +1751,12 @@
 
 &tlmm {
 	wakeup-parent = <&mpm>;
+
+	/* Pulled up, as in the vendor tree: the line was held low. */
+	nfc_clk_req: nfc-clk-req-state {
+		pins = "gpio86";
+		function = "gpio";
+		drive-strength = <2>;
+		bias-pull-up;
+	};
 };
diff --git a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
index 92ce096..dd40e00 100644
--- a/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/nxp-nci/i2c.c
@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <linux/acpi.h>
+#include <linux/clk.h>
 #include <linux/delay.h>
 #include <linux/i2c.h>
 #include <linux/interrupt.h>
@@ -308,6 +309,15 @@ static int nxp_nci_i2c_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 		return PTR_ERR(phy->gpiod_fw);
 	}
 
+	/* The clocks the board says the controller needs, if any. */
+	{
+		struct clk_bulk_data *clks;
+
+		r = devm_clk_bulk_get_all_enabled(dev, &clks);
+		if (r < 0)
+			return dev_err_probe(dev, r, "Failed to enable clocks\n");
+	}
+
 	r = nxp_nci_probe(phy, &client->dev, &i2c_phy_ops,
 			  NXP_NCI_I2C_MAX_PAYLOAD, &phy->ndev);
 	if (r < 0)
